      "Dismantling the Structural Reduction (Colleagues 13, 14, 16, 21): Tony's D4 and Maria's B4 never move simultaneously! Tony attacks D4 in m. 5 b3 (held across m. 6 b0-1); Maria attacks B4 on m. 6 b0 while Tony is stationary (oblique). On beat 2, Tony moves D4->Eb4 while Maria is stationary (oblique). By beat 3, Tony has already vacated D4. To synthesize a structural (D,B)->(C,C) contrary motion requires pasting together non-simultaneous pitches from beats 0 and 3, which is a contrapuntal impossibility.",
